# age-commit crash coverage (ledger `age-commit-crash-coverage-gap`):
# after a leading data fsync (flush-density gate conformance), a write
# is left UNCOMMITTED and the workload dwells 7s > the 5s age trigger,
# so the journal commits it on age alone — no fsync/sync is issued
# inside the dwell. Evidence: this workload's log segment must contain
# exactly 3 journal commits (data fsync + age commit + marker fsync) vs
# the control's 2 (see age_evidence.py; the law is stated in commit
# blocks — this kernel emits 2-3 FLUSH barriers per commit).

# define
test
foo
bar
zzz

# run
write zzz 0 4096
fsync zzz
write foo 0 4096
sleep 7
write bar 0 4096
checkpoint 1
